cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this repository, please cite the paper below together with the prior work it
  credits (see the priority note at the top of the paper).
title: "A machine-checked spectral floor for Pauli contextuality, and new configurations that attain it"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Donahue
    given-names: "Alexander S."
    alias: 0thernes
    affiliation: "0thernes LLC"
    email: "0_0@0thernes.art"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-8168-9648"
version: "1.1.1"
date-released: 2026-11-09
repository-code: "https://github.com/0thernes/hoggar-bound-lab"
url: "https://0thernes.github.io/hoggar-bound-lab/"
abstract: >-
  Lean 4 formalization, for every number of qubits and arbitrary sets of Pauli observables,
  of the spectral lower bound on the contextuality degree (first posted by B. W. Jonah,
  doi:10.5281/zenodo.23538829), with formally verified numerical corollaries. The bound is
  attained exactly when a pure state has Pauli expectation values of one modulus on the set and
  zero elsewhere. New configurations of this kind outside the classical families, with their
  exact contextuality degrees: 135 four-qubit observables with 1095 contexts (degree 75) and
  496 five-qubit observables with 10880 contexts (degree 480), both proved in Lean; and 8128
  seven-qubit observables with 2824192 contexts (degree 729344). A classification of the
  flat states obtained from T, controlled-S and CCZ gates on up to five qubits, an
  independent reproduction of the known values for two to five qubits, and a demonstration
  on the Tsotchke stack (Moonlab, quantum_geometric_tensor, quantum_rng, Eshkol).
keywords:
  - quantum contextuality
  - Pauli group
  - symplectic polar space
  - Kochen-Specker theorem
  - Clifford hierarchy
  - bent functions
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
